  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 gives customers complete per-model failure-rate data and keeps regulator submissions confidential, but sets no permanent limit and no sales stop, so a 5% failure rate only triggers review. S5 turns the 8-per-100k threshold into a notification and review trigger rather than a mandatory recall, leaving recall to regulator discretion. S3's six-year retrofit period and S4's 36-month suppression deadline sit inside the acceptable ranges."
